# The Gemini API key does NOT belong in this file, and this build no longer reads it from here.
#
# It used to. The Secrets Gradle plugin read GEMINI_API_KEY from this file and injected it into
# BuildConfig, which compiled it into classes.dex - so the credential shipped inside the APK and
# was recoverable by anyone who unzipped it. The plugin has been removed.
#
# The key now belongs to the AI backend, not the app:
#
#   1. Copy backend/.env.example to backend/.env  (gitignored - never commit a real key)
#   2. Set GEMINI_API_KEY there, or supply it as a real environment variable in your host
#   3. Run the backend:  node backend/server.mjs
#
# If you are deploying to a platform with a secret store (Cloud Run, Fly, Render, Railway, a VM),
# set GEMINI_API_KEY there instead of in any file. See backend/README.md.
#
# The only thing the Android build takes from the environment is the backend *URL*, which is not a
# secret:
#
#   gradlew :app:assembleRelease -PHANZISRS_AI_BACKEND_URL=https://ai.example.com